($\sim$$80\times$ lower), at \textbf{$0\%$ false-adapt} (adapt-precision $1.0$). It routes by
true regime exactly as the theory predicts: among harmful cells it adapts $0$ and freezes
them; among helpful cells it adapts almost all; on marginal cells it abstains (Tent: harmful
$0/63$ adapt/freeze, helpful $218/0$, $120$ abstentions on marginal). For SAR---whose
entropy-reset already prevents most collapse---\textsc{KGA} \emph{ties} always-adapt
($0.0018{=}0.0018$) and never does worse, consistent with the theory that the certificate's
value scales with how often detectable harm occurs. The mixing-ratio Pareto
(Fig.~\ref{fig:decisive}) makes the claim precise: \textsc{KGA} is on the regret-vs-mix
Pareto front, strictly beating both trivial policies once the harmful fraction exceeds
$p^\star\!\approx\!0.1$ (Tent/SAR) or $0$ (EATA), and tying always-adapt at $p{=}0$.

