\paragraph{Breadth across existing datasets, and uncertainty.} Re-running the certificate on
$62$ additional label-free anomaly-detection tasks (precomputed detector scores; no neural
retraining) stress-tests safety in a regime that is $85\%$ harmful: \textsc{KGA} makes $0$
false-adapt decisions and matches always-freeze (regret $0.0055$ vs always-adapt $0.051$, a
$9.3\times$ reduction), correctly refusing to adapt where the ensemble candidate hurts. It does
not \emph{beat} freezing here because almost nothing is helpful---the honest, correct behaviour,
and consistent with the knowability frontier (Thm.~\ref{thm:frontier}): this domain sits deep in the
knowably-harmful region. \emph{Corrected uncertainty quantification (per-condition).} An
earlier draft reported mixing-bootstrap intervals over a synthetic harmful-fraction
stream; we replace them with paired per-condition bootstrap CIs ($10^4$ resamples) with
Holm correction over the comparison family, computed on the real logged 65-cell
CIFAR-10-C data: \textsc{KGA} vs always-\emph{freeze} survives correction for all three
candidates ($\Delta\mathrm{regret}\approx-0.214$, 95\%~CI $[-0.245,-0.183]$,
$p\approx2\times10^{-20}$), while \textsc{KGA} vs always-\emph{adapt} is \emph{not}
significant on this helpful-dominated grid (Tent $+0.0001$, ns; EATA $\approx0$, ns;
SAR $+0.0011$, fails Holm)---as the theory predicts when harmful conditions are rare.
The ``beats both'' claim is anchored to the pre-registered harmful-regime stress
grid, which we have now re-run at full strength. \emph{Pre-registered $5$-seed
re-run (Protocol~A).} Following the frozen plan
(\texttt{research\_lock/STRESS\_GRID\_MULTISEED\_PROTOCOL\_A\_v1.yaml}, registered
before any result was observed), we replayed the identical $432$-condition CIFAR-10-C
grid across seeds $0$--$4$ and serialized every per-condition array, replacing the
old mixing bootstrap with per-condition \emph{paired} bootstrap CIs ($10^4$ resamples,
seeds pooled by per-condition mean) under Holm correction over the $6$-comparison
family. The pre-stated verdict is \textbf{STANDS}: \textsc{Tent} and \textsc{EATA}
each beat \emph{both} trivial policies after correction. Against always-\emph{freeze},
\textsc{KGA} cuts mean regret by $0.123$ (Tent; $95\%$~CI $[-0.138,-0.108]$),
$0.130$ (EATA; $[-0.145,-0.115]$) and $0.139$ (SAR; $[-0.154,-0.124]$); against
always-\emph{adapt} it wins for Tent ($-0.0064$, $[-0.0079,-0.0049]$) and EATA
($-0.0020$, $[-0.0028,-0.0013]$), all surviving Holm at $\alpha{=}0.05$
($p_{\mathrm{Holm}}{=}6\times10^{-4}$; between-seed regret SD ${\sim}2\times10^{-4}$).
The false-adapt rate (adapt with $B\le0$) is $0/2160$ for every candidate, far below
$\alpha{=}0.10$, and conformal $\varepsilon$ is stable across seeds (CV $2.7$--$6.8\%$).
\textsc{SAR} ties always-adapt as pre-stated ($+0.0012$, $[+0.0009,+0.0015]$, does
not beat): its harmful base rate ($0.07$--$0.12$) sits at/below $p^\star{\approx}0.1$,
so adaptation is almost always safe and \textsc{KGA}'s small abstention cost is not
repaid. This confirms the $p^\star$ regime law: per-seed, ``beats both'' is monotone
in the harmful fraction and single-threshold separable---every non-beating case
(\textsc{SAR}) has harmful fraction $\le0.116$, every beating case (\textsc{EATA},
\textsc{Tent}) $\ge0.234$ (\texttt{LOCKED\_ANALYSIS\_FINDINGS.md}). Additionally,
a first \emph{real-data audit} of the
Theorem~\ref{thm:conj1-dichotomy} machinery on the anomaly bank (6-detector panels,
46--52 usable tasks) behaves as proved: the falsifier rejects H on ${\sim}84\%$ of
tasks (correlated detectors---the diagnostic working, not failing), and where H passes,
relative-sign recovery is $0.78$ versus ${\approx}0.49$ (chance) where it is rejected;
advantage \emph{magnitudes} do not transfer under the bank's extreme class imbalance
($\pi_D\le0.06$), reported as a negative
(\texttt{theory\_v2/realdata/}, \texttt{REALDATA\_FINDINGS.md}).

\subsection{External validation: natural shift and ImageNet scale}\label{sec:external}

\paragraph{ImageNet-R, 48-condition light grid (single seed): the falsifier in charge.}
On ImageNet-R (200 classes, 30{,}000 images; severity$\times$composition$\times$batch$\times$update,
$48$ conditions, $288$ records, single commodity GPU) the regime is mild and weakly
detectable: harmful base rate $0.139$, mean benefit $+0.017$, best label-free harm
detectability AUC $0.662$. The multi-candidate diagnostic of
Theorem~\ref{thm:conj1-dichotomy} rejects the structural hypothesis H on \emph{all}
$48$ conditions ($\hat\tau\in[1.07,2.15]$ against threshold $\tau^\star{=}0.52$): the
TTA candidates are co-adapted, exactly the correlated-panel violation the falsifier
exists to catch, so the certified route abstains on $100\%$ of conditions---mandatory
under the theory, and consistent with the anomaly-bank audit
(\S\ref{sec:exp}). The honest cost of that validity is the forfeited mean oracle gain
of $+0.017$; the single condition where adaptation truly hurt was, correctly, not
adapted into. A smooth-drift fallback route commits conservatively ($7/48$
\textsc{freeze}, $41/48$ \textsc{abstain}; sign-bracket coverage $0.77$). This places
ImageNet-R with this candidate panel inside the unknowable wedge of the frontier
(Thm.~\ref{thm:frontier}): small margins, falsified structure, weak detectability.
Testing whether an \emph{independently trained} (non-co-adapted) panel passes H and
lets the sign certificate fire is the pre-registered next run. Single-seed, reported
as scoping evidence, not a headline
(\texttt{experiments/kbound/results/imagenetr\_kbound\_light\_mps\_internal/result\_f4a1293b.json}).

