fetches the data, and writes the table and figures.

\noindent\textbf{Environment.} Experiments use a \texttt{uv}/\texttt{venv} environment, Python
3.12, with the deep-TTA runs pinned to \texttt{torch 2.5.1}/\texttt{torchvision 0.20.1}; the
CPU-only stages need only \texttt{numpy/scipy/scikit-learn/matplotlib}, and \texttt{pdflatex}
compiles the paper. A \texttt{Dockerfile} builds the production inference API
(FastAPI/\texttt{uvicorn}, \texttt{python:3.11-slim} pinned by digest).

\noindent\textbf{Data.} CIFAR-10/100 are pulled via \texttt{torchvision}; the official CIFAR-10-C
corruptions are the Hendrycks--Dietterich set, Zenodo DOI \texttt{10.5281/zenodo.2535967}
(\texttt{CIFAR-10-C.tar}, md5 \texttt{56bf5dce}\dots), auto-downloaded and checksummed by
\texttt{scripts/fetch\_cifar\_c.py}.

\noindent\textbf{Determinism and honesty.} Single-run stages use fixed seeds; the locked
deep-TTA stress grid reports seeds $0$--$4$ with a split-conformal radius at
$\alpha=0.1$. The deep-TTA grid is \emph{pre-registered} (declared before any result is
observed) and reported in full, with no condition dropped. Every theorem ships a numerical
sanity-check script under \texttt{experiments/kbound/theory\_validation/}; all were re-run
from a clean environment and pass. Result manifests and locked CIFAR artifacts
(\texttt{result\_manifest.json}, \texttt{decisive\_tta\_results.json},
\texttt{LOCKED\_ANALYSIS\_RESULTS.json}, \texttt{per\_condition\_cifar10c\_*}) back every
reported number.

